content.text:
Zero skipped batches so far on the retry — the timeout is applying this time. It's at `ar`, the locale that failed first before.

**Fixed the margin.** `._pendo-text-custom` carries an inline `margin: 13px 0 0`, and it sits *inside* the form, so the existing survey rule — which zeroes top margins on the card's direct children — never reached it. Added to the survey block in [card.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/card.css):

```css
/* With no title above it, the leading block would double the card's top padding. */
._pendo-step-container-styles
  > :is(.pendo-survey-wrapper:first-child, ._pendo-close-guide:first-child + .pendo-survey-wrapper)
  > :first-child {
  margin-block-start: var(--pendo-space-0);
}
```

The two-arm `:is()` is what encodes your "no title or subtitle" condition: it only matches when the survey wrapper actually leads the card. The second arm exists because the close button is a real DOM child that precedes the form even though it's absolutely positioned — a plain `:first-child` would miss it. If a title or subtitle is present, it becomes the first child instead, neither arm matches, and the 13px stays.

Browser-verified: the question text now aligns with the top of the glyph swatch rather than sitting 13px below it. Checks and all 18 tests pass.

Still running: the API-doc translation retry. The earlier `vp run` attempt accumulated 9 timed-out batches because `vp run` isolates task env and silently dropped my raised `DOCS_TRANSLATION_TIMEOUT_MS` — it kept using the 120s default. Invoking `build-api-locales.ts` directly picks it up. Once that's clean I'll run `check:publish`.

