content.text:
Fixed and browser-verified with your exact `<strong>` markup.

**Cause:** `._pendo-text-bold` is a bare class at specificity (0,1,0). The banner block's `:is(:scope, [class*="instui"]):not(…):is(…) :is(._pendo-simple-text, [class*="_pendo-text-"])` reaches (0,4,0) and sets `font-weight` to the body weight. Your `<strong>` carries *both* classes, so the higher-specificity rule wins and flattens it to 400. The inline `font-weight: 700` can't save it either, since the build stamps `!important` on every declaration.

**Fix** — re-assert the inline variants immediately after the blanket rule in both banner typography blocks (base and the compact container-query twin) in [text.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/text.css):

```css
/* Re-assert after the rule above, which outranks the bare variant classes. */
:is(._pendo-text-bold, ._pendo-text-italic) {
  font-weight: var(--instui-component-text-content-important-font-weight);
}
```

Equal specificity to the blanket rule, so source order decides — which is why placement after it is load-bearing. I included `._pendo-text-italic` because it sets `font-weight` too and was being flattened identically.

Worth noting this was **not** introduced by the banner-survey work — regular `lightboxBlank` banners have had the same flattened bold since the banner typography block was written. Widening the selector just made it visible on surveys.

Checks and all 18 tests pass.
